{"ld": 1962, "paper": "SP769", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Increase Legislative Access to Department of Corrections Facilities and to Direct the Commissioner to Establish Rules Regarding Legislator Access to Correctional and Detention Facilities (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "s-duson-jill", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-beebe-center-anne", "s-bennett-richard", "h-hasenfus-tavis", "h-milliken-nina", "s-talbot-ross-rachel"], "committee_code": "CJPS", "committee_name": "Criminal Justice and Public Safety", "summary": {"text": "This bill establishes the Office of the Corrections Ombudsman. The office is responsible for:\n\n1. Receiving, investigating and resolving complaints and suggestions from certain incarcerated persons and from staff of the Department of Corrections; 2. Providing information to the Governor, the department and its staff, the Legislature, certain incarcerated persons and their families and the public; 3. Promoting public awareness and understanding of the problems and challenges of incarceration; 4. Identifying systemic issues and responses upon which the department, the Governor and the Legislature may act; and 5. Ensuring compliance with relevant statutes, rules, regulations and policies concerning correctional facilities, services, staff and treatment of certain incarcerated persons.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0769&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2026-04-19", "governor_action": "Unsigned", "governor_action_date": "2026-04-19"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1962)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0769&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-577)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0769&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}, {"label": "Amendment C-B (S-578)", 